      "text": "To determine the remainder when the sum \\(1 + 7 + 13 + 19 + \\cdots + 253 + 259\\) is divided by 6, we start by identifying the pattern in the sequence. The sequence is an arithmetic series where the first term \\(a = 1\\) and the common difference \\(d = 6\\).\n\nThe general term of the arithmetic sequence can be written as:\n\\[ a_n = a + (n-1)d \\]\n\nSubstituting \\(a = 1\\) and \\(d = 6\\), the \\(n\\)-th term becomes:\n\\[ a_n = 1 + (n-1) \\cdot 6 = 6n - 5 \\]\n\nWe need to find the number of terms in the sequence. The last term \\(a_n = 259\\):\n\\[ 259 = 6n - 5 \\]\n\\[ 264 = 6n \\]\n\\[ n = 44 \\]\n\nThus, there are 44 terms in the sequence. We now need to find the remainder when the sum of these terms is divided by 6. To do this, we first find the sum of the entire arithmetic series using the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series:\n\\[ S_n = \\frac{n}{2} (a + l) \\]\nwhere \\( n \\) is the number of terms, \\( a \\) is the first term, and \\( l \\) is the last term.\n\nHere, \\( n = 44 \\), \\( a = 1 \\), and \\( l = 259 \\). Plugging these values into the formula gives:\n\\[ S_{44} = \\frac{44}{2} (1 + 259) \\]\n\\[ S_{44} = 22 \\cdot 260 \\]\n\\[ S_{44} = 5720 \\]\n\nNext, we find the remainder when \\( 5720 \\) is divided by 6. We perform the division:\n\\[ 5720 \\div 6 \\]\n\\[ 5720 \\div 6 = 953 \\text{ remainder } 2 \\]\n\nThus, the remainder when the sum \\(1 + 7 + 13 + 19 + \\cdots + 253 + 259\\) is divided by 6 is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{2}\n\\]",
