      "text": "To find the remainder when the sum \\(1 + 7 + 13 + 19 + \\cdots + 253 + 259\\) is divided by 6, we need to first find the sum of this arithmetic series and then find the remainder of that sum when divided by 6.\n\n### Step 1: Find the number of terms in the series\nThe series is \\(1, 7, 13, 19, \\ldots, 253, 259\\). It is an arithmetic sequence with the first term \\(a = 1\\) and common difference \\(d = 6\\).\n\nThe general formula for the \\(n\\)-th term of an arithmetic sequence is:\n\\[ a_n = a + (n-1)d \\]\n\nGiven the last term, 259, we can find the number of terms, \\(n\\):\n\\[ 259 = 1 + (n-1) \\cdot 6 \\]\n\\[ 259 = 1 + 6n - 6 \\]\n\\[ 259 = 6n - 5 \\]\n\\[ 264 = 6n \\]\n\\[ n = 44 \\]\n\nSo, there are 44 terms in the sequence.\n\n### Step 2: Calculate the sum of the series\nThe sum \\(S_n\\) of the first \\(n\\) terms of an arithmetic series is given by:\n\\[ S_n = \\frac{n}{2} \\left(2a + (n-1)d\\right) \\]\n\nHere, \\(n = 44\\), \\(a = 1\\), and \\(d = 6\\):\n\\[ S_{44} = \\frac{44}{2} \\left(2 \\cdot 1 + (44-1) \\cdot 6\\right) \\]\n\\[ S_{44} = 22 \\left(2 + 43 \\cdot 6\\right) \\]\n\\[ S_{44} = 22 \\left(2 + 258\\right) \\]\n\\[ S_{44} = 22 \\cdot 260 \\]\n\\[ S_{44} = 5720 \\]\n\n### Step 3: Find the remainder when the sum is divided by 6\nTo find the remainder when 5720 is divided by 6, perform the division:\n\\[ 5720 \\div 6 = 953 \\text{ with a remainder of } 2. \\]\n\\[ 5720 = 6 \\times 953 + 2 \\]\n\nThus, the remainder when 5720 is divided by 6 is 2.\n\nSo the answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{2}\n\\]",
